This is a production-grade, modular Web Application Firewall (WAF) designed for modern ASP.NET Core applications. It is engineered with high-performance concurrent data structures, strict input sanitization, dynamic OS-level firewall blocking, and architectural separation of concerns.

---

### Architecture Diagram

```
                       +---------------------------------------+
                       |          Incoming HTTP Request         |
                       +---------------------------------------+
                                           |
                                           v
                       +---------------------------------------+
                       |             WafMiddleware             |
                       +---------------------------------------+
                                           |
                    [Step 1: Check IP]     |
                                           v
                       +---------------------------------------+
                       |        IIPReputationEngine            | <--- (Blocks Known Blacklisted IPs)
                       +---------------------------------------+
                                           |
                    [Step 2: Check Rate]   |
                                           v
                       +---------------------------------------+
                       |     Sliding Window Rate Limiter       | <--- (Checks Requests/Min Threshold)
                       +---------------------------------------+
                                           |
                    [Step 3: Inspect Payload]
                                           v
                       +---------------------------------------+
                       |          IRequestInspector            | <--- (Scans Headers, Query, & Body)
                       +---------------------------------------+
                                           |
                    [Anomaly Detected]     | [All Checks Pass]
                                           |
                                           v
                       +---------------------------------------+
                       |      IIncidentResponseSubsystem       |
                       |  - Structural Log Violations          |
                       |  - Dynamic OS Firewall Rules (IPTable)|
                       +---------------------------------------+
```

---

### Project Structure

1. **Interfaces**: Decoupled contract definitions.
2. **HTTP Request Inspector**: Signature-based SQLi scanning engine.
3. **Rate Limiting & IP Reputation Engine**: Sliding window rate-limiter and threat scoring matrix.
4. **Incident Response Subsystem**: Log defense and dynamic Linux/Windows system firewall controller.
5. **WAF Middleware**: The pipeline orchestrator.

---

### 1. Architectural Interfaces

These interfaces establish a clean, testable contract layout for the WAF components.

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http;
using System.Net;

namespace ModularWaf.Core
{
    public interface IRequestInspector
    {
        Task<(bool IsMalicious, string MatchedRule, string ViolationSnippet)> InspectAsync(HttpContext context);
    }

    public interface IIPReputationEngine
    {
        bool IsIPBlocked(IPAddress clientIp);
        bool TrackRequestAndCheckRateLimit(IPAddress clientIp);
        void IncrementViolationScore(IPAddress clientIp, int severityScore);
        int GetViolationScore(IPAddress clientIp);
        void WhitelistIP(IPAddress clientIp);
    }

    public interface IIncidentResponder
    {
        Task HandleViolationAsync(IPAddress clientIp, string violationType, string details, int criticalScore);
    }
}
```

